ection":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:0deb5c92ddcec92d7784189c42a0916e75ed1c17017525584fd74245b7f4c924","file":"preprints/Conditional-permutations-in-a-revealed-switching-environment-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":11,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1d514b84c5a25aa919a469c66b3ebb9a2557dec8e93a4a1db3ebe208135d37df","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Conditional-permutations-in-a-revealed-switching-environment-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:0deb5c92ddcec92d7784189c42a0916e75ed1c17017525584fd74245b7f4c924","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Conditional-permutations-in-a-revealed-switching-environment-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L11"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:methods}\nLet $n=2^d$, and start the shuffle from any deterministic deck.\nAfter $J(s_0+1)$ sweeps, where $s_0=400$ and $J=40000$, the conditional free-slot law defined above satisfies\n\\[\n \\sup_{\\text{initial layouts}}\\E_{\\mathcal E}\n       \\|\\nu_{\\mathcal E}-U_{n/2}\\|_{\\TV}\\longrightarrow0\n       \\qquad(d\\longrightarrow\\infty).\n\\]\nConsequently the full-deck law approaches uniform, uniformly in the starting deck, after $16\\,040\\,400d$ physical shuffles. For every integer $t\\ge0$, after $t$ physical shuffles the full-deck distance from uniform is at least\n$1-2^{tn/2}/n!$. Thus the full-deck mixing time is of order $d$."}
